From 8f4b2d8e7f18b5feae343cfa161a1864d6f503ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:06:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Do not memcpy from a NULL array when growing an empty one

lshpack_arr_init is a memset, so a fresh lshpack_arr has els == NULL,
off == 0 and nelem == 0. The first lshpack_arr_push therefore takes the
malloc path and calls

    memcpy(new_els, arr->els + arr->off, sizeof(arr->els[0]) * arr->nelem)

as memcpy(new_els, NULL + 0, 0). Nothing is copied, but NULL + 0 is
undefined arithmetic (C17 6.5.6p8) and memcpy's source is declared
non-null, so it is undefined twice over.

It is reached on the first dynamic-table insert of every decoder, which
is to say on the first request with an indexed field that any HTTP/2
connection carries. All four test_hpack variants report it under
-fsanitize=undefined:

    lshpack.c:236:5: runtime error: null pointer passed as argument 2,
                     which is declared to never be null

Guarding the copy on nelem leaves every other path untouched: when the
array has elements, els is not NULL and the copy runs exactly as before.
---
 .gitignore | 1 +
 lshpack.c  | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 .gitignore

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9137dd5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+build-ubsan/
diff --git a/lshpack.c b/lshpack.c
index 902aa8a..7c7d4eb 100644
--- a/lshpack.c
+++ b/lshpack.c
@@ -233,7 +233,8 @@ lshpack_arr_push (struct lshpack_arr *arr, uintptr_t val)
     new_els = malloc(n * sizeof(arr->els[0]));
     if (!new_els)
         return -1;
-    memcpy(new_els, arr->els + arr->off, sizeof(arr->els[0]) * arr->nelem);
+    if (arr->nelem)
+        memcpy(new_els, arr->els + arr->off, sizeof(arr->els[0]) * arr->nelem);
     free(arr->els);
     arr->off = 0;
     arr->els = new_els;
-- 
